045585 true] [17592186403563 1072 #uuid "bb2d08ab-7e1f-579d-8314-e037ebc00133" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403563 1074 "The horizontal asymptote of $y={2}^{x}$ is $y=0.$ The vertical translation $y={2}^{x}+c$ shifts the asymptote to $y=c.$\n\nIn the graph above, the horizontal asymptote is $y=-3.$ Therefore, $c=-3.$" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403564 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403565 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403564 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403566 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403564 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403567 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403564 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403568 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403564 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403569 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403564 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403564 1077 "selection" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403564 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403567 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403564 1080 #uuid "117f36b7-d2dd-58cf-81f2-744857f29ebf" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403565 1081 "y={2}^{x}-2" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403565 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403565 1084 #uuid "760d4f2f-67c3-578b-90ce-e44b5cc0e475" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403566 1081 "y=-3({2}^{x})" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403566 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403566 1084 #uuid "a42ff124-ce1b-58ec-a4c4-728cb4b536df" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403567 1081 "y={2}^{x}-3" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403567 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403567 1084 #uuid "9bb95f56-7efa-56a4-ab5b-5f4220d4b140" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403568 1081 "y={3}^{x}-4" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403568 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403568 1084 #uuid "840799e0-019f-5e56-960e-e4dce9f6a43e" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403569 1081 "y=3({2}^{x})" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403569 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403569 1084 #uuid "97c4002b-68c4-5b92-bb46-3a3c52c7bbac" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403570 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403571 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403570 1069 "q-72345" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403570 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403570 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the line $y=x$ and the curve $y={x}^{3},$ in the first quadrant?\n\nI. It is a type I region\nII. It is a type II region\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403570 1072 #uuid "d94b1132-4667-52b0-83fe-bd8235741b13" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403570 1074 "First, notice that\n\n$$\ny={x}^{3}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt[3]{y}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/1d/1d1c1cbe30e6f612f824adc76d712a98194ffccc5edefc11cccdaf07204513ba.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le x}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{y}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403571 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403572 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403571 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403573 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403571 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403574 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403571 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403575 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403571 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403576 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403571 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403571 1077 "selection" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403571 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403575 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403571 1080 #uuid "1886eec5-845d-5de6-8b01-c5885246a233" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403572 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403572 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403572 1084 #uuid "cebe51cf-7c64-56b5-90cf-d131aa350434" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403573 1081 "I only" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403573 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403573 1084 #uuid "bb98efc4-1808-5a18-907a-2ed362b46813" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403574 1081 "III only" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403574 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403574 1084 #uuid "715194f5-7e2b-5553-92e1-418bb1db22f9" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403575 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403575 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403575 1084 #uuid "52989cfd-9a0b-5436-a602-9bec29db010b" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403576 1081 "II only" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403576 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403576 1084 #uuid "23c11e6d-f7bd-5794-99cd-309344d7fab8" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403577 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403578 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403577 1069 "q-72412" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403577 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403577 1071 "At which points on the curve ${y}^{2}-4xy=-5{x}^{2}+1$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $i?$" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403577 1072 #uuid "49dc4b38-854b-53b5-ba44-1bf47c27ef1c" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403577 1074 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-4xy & =-5{x}^{2}+1 \\\\ {y}^{2}-4xy+5{x}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)={y}^{2}-4xy+5{x}^{2}$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=1.$ \n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(x,y)={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y) & ={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}-4xy+5{x}^{2})i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}-4xy+5{x}^{2})j \\\\  & =2(y-2x)\\,i-(10x-4y)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $i$, we must have $t\\cdot i=0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot i & =0 \\\\ (2(y-2x)\\,i-(10x-4y)\\,j)\\cdot i & =0 \\\\ 2(y-2x) & =0 \\\\ y & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y=2x$ into the equation of our curve gives:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-4xy+5{x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ (2x)^{2}-4x(2x)+5{x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-8{x}^{2}+5{x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally:\n\n- If $x=1$, we get $y=2$ and the corresponding point is $(1,2).$\n\n- If $x=-1$, we get $y=-2$ and the corresponding point is $(-1,-2).$" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403578 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403579 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403578 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403580 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403578 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403581 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403578 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403582 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403578 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403583 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403578 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403578 1077 "selection" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403578 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403581 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403578 1080 #uuid "22c59322-d13f-5287-a0fa-c2f86091a95e" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403579 1081 "$(3,2)$ and $(-1,3)$" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403579 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403579 1084 #uuid "b3b898a6-e9f5-51f8-8993-b6f0322af5e6" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403580 1081 "$(1,1)$ and $(-1,-1)$" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403580 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403580 1084 #uuid "3acac861-9675-5531-8e0f-29301bd84beb" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403581 1081 "$(1,2)$ and $(-1,-2)$" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403581 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403581 1084 #uuid "879099ba-26c3-5eca-b156-1546984f09e1" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403582 1081 "$(-1,2)$ and $(1,-2)$" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403582 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403582 1084 #uuid "56e7a278-62d5-5448-adb4-7672d93764ee" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403583 1081 "$(1,3)$ and $(3,-2)$" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403583 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403583 1084 #uuid "c66b876c-2af7-5756-8122-0570c4918dbd" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403584 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403585 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403584 1069 "q-72491" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403584 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403584 1071 "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403584 1072 #uuid "307a31ed-3320-5bc6-9033-1067b69032de" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403584 1074 "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${a}_{43}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${c}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ are **not** in row echelon form." 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403585 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403586 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403585 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403587 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403585 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403588 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403585 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403589 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403585 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403590 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403585 1076 #e