723 1069 "q-73866" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403723 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403723 1071 "For the elliptic paraboloid $\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}=z+5$, the section in the plane $\\sqrt{3}x-2y=2\\sqrt{3}$ is a parabola. \nFind the vertex of the projection of this parabola onto $xz$-plane." 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403723 1072 #uuid "cc9a60c0-9b27-537d-8f7e-b89ae32845f5" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403723 1074 "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xz$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $y.$ First, we solve for $y$ in the equation of the plane, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}x-2y=2\\sqrt{3}\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-2)}{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $y$ into the equation of the paraboloid, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-2)}{2})}^{2} & =z+5 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{3(x-2)^{2}}{4} & =z+5 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}+4x+4}{4}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}-12x+12}{4} & =z+5 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}-8x+16}{4} & =z+5 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+4 & =z+5 \\\\ z & ={x}^{2}-2x-1 \\\\ z & =({x}^{2}-2x+1)-2 \\\\ z & ={(x-1)}^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the vertex of the projection onto $xz$-plane is $(1,-2).$" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403725 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403726 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403727 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403728 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403729 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1077 "selection" 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403725 13194139533493 17592186045585 true] [17592186403724 1080 #uuid "635cbbf9-c9f6-5df5-ac89